  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "imperative: affirmative for directions (Go straight/Turn left)",
      "title_form": "Imperativo afirmativo para dar direcciones",
      "title_target": "Affirmative Imperative for Directions",
      "description_md_form": "Para dar direcciones en inglés, usamos el **imperativo afirmativo**: la forma base del verbo, sin sujeto. Es directo y claro.\n\n**Estructura:** `Verbo base + complemento`\n\nEjemplos:\n- `Go straight.` (Sigue recto)\n- `Turn left.` (Gira a la izquierda)\n- `Look at the map.` (Mira el mapa)\n\nUsamos `then` (luego) para ordenar los pasos: `Go straight, then turn left.`\n\nEl imperativo es igual para todas las personas (you, we, they). No cambia la forma del verbo. Es la manera más común y educada de dar instrucciones de camino.",
      "description_md_target": "To give directions in English, we use the **affirmative imperative**: the base form of the verb, without a subject. It is direct and clear.\n\n**Structure:** `Base verb + complement`\n\nExamples:\n- `Go straight.`\n- `Turn left.`\n- `Look at the map.`\n\nWe use `then` to order the steps: `Go straight, then turn left.`\n\nThe imperative is the same for all persons (you, we, they). The verb form does not change. It is the most common and polite way to give directions.",
      "grammar_structure": "Base verb + complement (then + base verb + complement)",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "imperative_affirmative",
        "headers": [
          "Persona",
          "Verbo",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
